# Patch: register `osdev` as a valid OS suffix in
# gmp-6.2.1's bundled `configfsf.sub`, so cross-building
# gmp with `--host=aarch64-osdev` is accepted.
#
# Background.  gmp ships TWO config.sub layers:
#   - `config.sub`     — gmp-specific wrapper for aliases
#                         like `pentium4 -> i786`.  Delegates
#                         the canonicalisation arm to ...
#   - `configfsf.sub`  — a stock GNU config.sub copy.  This
#                         is where the OS recognition list
#                         lives, so the patch lands here.
#
# Without this hunk gmp's `configure --host=aarch64-osdev`
# aborts with:
#
#   Invalid configuration `aarch64-osdev': OS `osdev' not
#   recognized
#
# before any compiler flag is consulted.  Adding `osdev*`
# to the recognised-OS case is a one-line additive change;
# the canonical form gmp then sees is the same
# `aarch64-unknown-osdev` that gcc and binutils receive
# (because both of their config.subs have the same edit,
# via vendor/gcc-aarch64-osdev.patch and
# vendor/binutils-aarch64-osdev.patch respectively).
#
# Companion patches in the same chapter:
#   vendor/mpfr-aarch64-osdev.patch  — older `-osdev*`
#                                       prefix form
#   vendor/mpc-aarch64-osdev.patch   — same bare form
#
# Apply with:
#   patch -p1 -d vendor/gmp-6.2.1/ < \
#       vendor/gmp-aarch64-osdev.patch
#
# Re-application is gated by the marker file
# `vendor/gmp-6.2.1/.patched-osdev` written by
# scripts/fetch_gcc_prereqs.sh after a successful apply.
#
# Chapter 132e (cross-building gmp/mpfr/mpc for the
# aarch64-osdev guest sysroot).
#
--- a/configfsf.sub
+++ b/configfsf.sub
@@ -1709,6 +1709,7 @@
 	     | udi* | lites* | ieee* | go32* | aux* | hcos* \
 	     | chorusrdb* | cegcc* | glidix* \
 	     | cygwin* | msys* | pe* | moss* | proelf* | rtems* \
+	     | osdev* \
 	     | midipix* | mingw32* | mingw64* | mint* \
 	     | uxpv* | beos* | mpeix* | udk* | moxiebox* \
 	     | interix* | uwin* | mks* | rhapsody* | darwin* \
